  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: DiscCare 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "When asked what types of new treatments families hope to see, you share
    that your wife\u2019s current treatment causes severe fatigue and nausea, and
    you hope future treatments will allow patients to better enjoy everyday life.\n\n<b>How
    could this feedback help in early research?</b>"
  explanation: "While caregivers may not be directly involved in clinical studies,
    their voices can still shape what scientists focus on in early research. By sharing
    what patients go through\u2014like fatigue, pain, or emotional challenges\u2014they
    help researchers understand what kinds of treatments could make the biggest difference.
    Their input reminds researchers that it\u2019s not just about finding new ways
    to fight cancer, but about helping patients live better and feel better, too."
  correctAnswer: It may help researchers focus on treatments that fight cancer more
    directly and cause fewer side effects.
  incorrectAnswer1: It could change how doctors prescribe existing treatment options
    to patients.
  incorrectAnswer2: It will help research teams decide which patients and how many
    will be selected for a clinical trial.
  incorrectAnswer3: It could cause new treatments to get approved and become available
    to all patients faster.
  questionRole: Caregiver
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Discovery
